# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Model weights - NEVER commit. Multi-gigabyte, third-party licensed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.gguf
*.ggml
*.safetensors
*.bin
*.pt
*.pth
models/
model/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Clean-room source and build tree
#
# clean-room/llama.cpp is a checkout of upstream llama.cpp; it belongs in
# upstream's repository, not this one. What this project actually owns is
# patches/, which reconstructs it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
clean-room/llama.cpp/
clean-room/build/
clean-room/*.log
release-candidate/llama.cpp/
release-candidate/build/
build/
build-*/
out/
cmake-build-*/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build artifacts and debug symbols
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.obj
*.o
*.a
*.lib
*.exp
*.ilk
*.pdb
*.dll
*.exe
*.so
*.dylib
*.res
*.idb
*.tlog
*.ipdb
*.iobj
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
compile_commands.json
.ninja_deps
.ninja_log
*.ninja

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Crash dumps and profiler output - can embed memory contents and local paths
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.dmp
*.mdmp
*.etl
*.nvvp
*.nsight-cuprof-report
*.ncu-rep
*.qdrep
*.sqlite

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Benchmark and session output
#
# Raw logs contain absolute local paths, process ids, and machine identifiers.
# Curated results that are meant to be published are force-added:
#     git add -f benchmark/results/<name>/SUMMARY.md
#     git add -f benchmark/results/<name>/results.csv
#
# tests/results/ carries the same shape of data for the real-use, quality-eval and
# perplexity-matrix harnesses: real prompts, real model output, and machine-specific
# environment JSON. Same rule - curate and force-add what you want published.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
benchmark/results/
tests/results/
launcher/sessions/
*.stdout.log
*.stderr.log
*.tokens.txt
*.counters.txt
*.perf.txt

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Evaluation corpora
#
# Derived data, not source: extracts of this project's own documentation, of
# llama.cpp's C/C++ sources, and hand-written Thai prose. Excluded because they
# are large, because one of them is a verbatim extract of upstream source, and
# because they are not a standard benchmark anyone should treat as canonical.
# docs/QUALITY_REPORT.md describes what they are so you can assemble your own.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
tests/corpora/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets - none are used by this project; these patterns are a safety net
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.pfx
*.p12
*_token
*_secret
credentials.json
secrets.json
.netrc
.npmrc
.pypirc

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor and OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo
*.swp
*~
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Scratch
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
tmp/
temp/
scratch/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Internal Phase G tracking records
#
# These document the productization process itself, not the product: they name
# the private local research workspace path repeatedly (D:\llm-v0\...) and are
# meaningful mainly to whoever ran that phase, not to a user of the repo.
# Per PUBLIC_RELEASE_CHECKLIST.md item 6.2, they are kept locally and not
# published. Force-add individually if you decide otherwise.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/PRODUCTIZATION_BASELINE.md
/PRODUCTIZATION_STATE.json
/PRODUCTIZATION_LOG.md
/PRODUCTIZATION_FINAL_REPORT.md
